AI Swing Trading Signal Generator

A machine learning-powered stock trading system that scans major stocks and ETFs to identify high-probability swing trade opportunities.

The model analyzes over 10 years of market data and uses technical indicators, trend analysis, volatility measurements, and market sentiment data to predict whether a stock is likely to move higher over the next 5 trading days.

Features
Downloads 10 years of historical market data using Yahoo Finance
Uses XGBoost classification to predict short-term price direction
Evaluates multiple stocks simultaneously:
SPY
QQQ
AAPL
MSFT
NVDA
AMD
META
AMZN
Incorporates market sentiment using VIX data
Calculates technical indicators including:
RSI
EMA20 / EMA50 / EMA200
Relative Strength vs SPY
Volume Ratios
Volatility
Momentum Returns
Distance from 52-Week High
Generates confidence-based BUY signals
Includes built-in backtesting and performance reporting
Machine Learning Features

The model evaluates market conditions using:

Trend strength
Momentum
Volume activity
Volatility
Market regime
Relative market performance
Fear/greed conditions through VIX analysis

Each day is classified as:

1 = Positive return expected within 5 trading days
0 = No positive return expected
Model Training

The system:

Builds a combined dataset from all selected tickers
Creates engineered features from technical indicators
Trains an XGBoost classifier
Tests predictions on unseen historical data
Filters trades using a minimum confidence threshold (75%)
Performance Analysis

After training, the script automatically generates:

Classification Report
Precision / Recall / F1 Scores
Feature Importance Rankings
Historical Backtest Results
Average Trade Return
Win Rate
Profit Factor
Live Signal Generation

The latest market data is evaluated in real time and each ticker receives:

Plain Text
SPY 81.4% BUY
QQQ 78.2% BUY
AAPL 61.7% NO TRADE
NVDA 84.9% BUY

Only predictions above the confidence threshold are considered trade candidates.

Tech Stack
Python
Pandas
NumPy
XGBoost
Scikit-Learn
Yahoo Finance API (yfinance)
